                  "title": "Definitions",
                  "pages": "หน้า 2–6",
                  "text": "Adverse drug events: ADEs\n▪ Any untoward occurrence that may present during\ntreatment with a pharmaceutical product but that\ndoes not necessarily have a causal relation to the\ntreatment\nPSAP 2015\n• Adverse drug reactions: ADRs\n▪ A response to a drug that is noxious and unintended\nand occurs at doses normally used in man for the\nprophylaxis, diagnosis, or therapy of disease or for\nmodification of physiological function (WHO)\nDrug allergy\n▪ Are a hypersensitive reaction of the immune system\nto certain medications we may take.\nPSAP 2015\n• Side effects\n▪ Unintended effect occurring at normal dose related\nto the pharmacological properties.\nDrug-related problems: DRPs\n▪ An event or circumstance involving drug therapy that\nactually or potentially interferes with desired health\noutcomes\n• ADR\nSide\neffect\nVS\n• Medication errors\n▪ Any preventable event that may cause or lead to\ninappropriate medication use or patient harm while\nthe medication is in the control of the health care\nprofessional, patient, or consumer (NCC MERP)\nPSAP 2015"
