                  "title": "Phase of treatment",
                  "pages": "หน้า 15–16",
                  "text": "Response = modest improvement in symptoms severity after 1‐2 weeks of treatment\nReduction ≥ 20% in total HAM‐D\nReduction ≥ 50% from baseline symptoms\n• 25‐49% = partial response\n• <25% = nonresponse\nRemission HAM‐D ≤ 7‐12 or MADRS ≤ 10‐12\nCure ?\n• Phase of\ntreatment\nDuration of phase Objectives\nAcute 8-16 weeks, until symptom\nremission\n▪ Address patient safety\n▪ Treat to symptom remission\nand improvement\nMaintenance 6-24 months following the\nacute phase (or longer if\nclinically indicated)\n▪ Maintain symptomatic\nremission\n▪ Restore functioning and\nquality of life to premorbid\nlevels\n▪ Prevent recurrence\n▪ Consolidate gains during\ntreatment discontinuation\nCANMAT guideline 2023"
