                  "text": "Classification of H1 antihistamine\nAn Bras Dermatol. 2010;85(2):195-210.\n• ■ Basic structure requirements\nAr1\nPhenyl\nAr2\nPhenyl\nPyridyl\nThienyl\nR\nCH3 (methyl)\nC=O\nC\nN\n• ■ Ethanolamines (Aminoalkyl ethers)\n■ Alkylamine (Monoaminopropyl)\n■ Ethylenediamines\n■ Phenothiazines\n■ Piperazine\n■ Piperidine\n• ■ Ethanolamines (Aminoalkyl ethers)\nDiphenhydramine HCl\nBromodiphenhydramine HCl\nChlorodiphenhydramine HCl\n• ■ Ethanolamines (Aminoalkyl ethers)\nOrphenadrine citrate\nBenztropine mesylate\n• ■ Ethanolamines (Aminoalkyl ethers)\nDimenhydrinate\n8-chlorotheophyllinate (theoclate) salt of diphenhydramine\nDoxylamine Carbinoxamine\nPyridyl group\n• ■ Alkylamine (Monoaminopropyl)\nChlorpheniraminePheniramine\nBrompheniramine\n(+) isomer potent than (-) isomer\n• ■ Alkylamine (Monoaminopropyl)\nTriprolidine\nAcrivastine\nPyrrolidine ring\n• ■ Piperazine\nCyclizine\nPrototype\n• ■ Piperazine\n(Active metabolite)\n• ■ Phenothiazine\nPromethazine\nPhenothiazine\n• ■ Piperidine\nCyproheptadine\n(Active metabolite)\n(CYP3A4, 2D6)\n• ■ Piperidine\nTerfenadine\nProdrug\nFexofenadine\nActive drug\nAstemizole\nCYP450"
