            {
              "title": "IRRITABLE BOWEL",
              "pages": "หน้า 1",
              "text": "SYNDROMES"
            },
            {
              "title": "Introduction",
              "pages": "หน้า 2",
              "text": "▪ A functional bowel disorder in which abdominal pain is\nassociated with defecation (diarrhea and constipation) or\na change in bowel habit with features of disordered\ndefecation and distention\n▪ One of the most common chronic disorders causing\npatients to seek medical therapy\n▪ Female : male >>> 3:1 (high incidence; white population)"
            },
            {
              "title": "Pathophysiology",
              "pages": "หน้า 3",
              "text": "▪ Cause remains incomplete\n▪ Previously, cause from psychiatric or phychosomatic\n▪ More recently, psychologic stress is a factor NOT a\ncause\n▪ Activation of gut nociceptors due to ischemia or infection\n▪ Excitability of neurons in dorsal horn of spinal cord\n▪ Neurotransmitter abnormalities: higher level of  5 -HT3, 5-\nHT4 in colon >> trigger both GI smooth muscle contraction\nand relaxation\n▪ Altered colonic motility"
            },
            {
              "title": "Clinical presentation",
              "pages": "หน้า 5",
              "text": "The signs and symptoms of IBS\nvary. The most common include:\n▪ Abdominal pain, cramping or\nbloating that is typically relieved\nor partially relieved by passing a\nbowel movement\n▪ Excess gas\n▪ Diarrhea or constipation —\nsometimes alternating bouts of\ndiarrhea and constipation\n▪ Mucus in the stool"
            },
            {
              "title": "Alarm symptoms",
              "pages": "หน้า 6",
              "text": "▪ Weight loss\n▪ GI bleeding\n▪ Anemia\n▪ Fever\n▪ Frequent noctural symptoms\n** extensive testing is unnecessary in patients < 50\nyears and no alarm symptoms **"
            },
            {
              "title": "Diagnosis",
              "pages": "หน้า 7–8",
              "text": "คำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)"
            },
            {
              "title": "Type of IBS",
              "pages": "หน้า 9",
              "text": "▪ IBS-D (Diarrhea-predominant)\n▪ IBS-C (Constipation-predominant)\n▪ IBS-M (Mixed)\n▪ IBS-U (Unspecified)\nคำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)"
            },
            {
              "title": "Non-pharmacologic treatment",
              "pages": "หน้า 10",
              "text": "▪ Dietary intervention\n▪ CP- IBS: increase consumption of fiber >> slowly increase,\nlarge dose of fiber can lead to abdominal gas and bloating\n▪ Psyllium-based products can be used (first line therapy for\nCP-IBS)\n▪ Prebiotic and probiotic (unclear)\n▪ Patient education\n▪ Exercise (all type IBS)\n▪ Help patients discover triggers that may exacerbate IBS\nsymptoms\n▪ Educate patients that IBS is benign in nature\nคำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)"
            },
            {
              "title": "Pharmacologic treatment",
              "pages": "หน้า 11–21",
              "text": "Treatment of abdominal pain\n▪ Antispasmodics and peppermint oil\n▪ Effective in reducing abdominal pain in patients with IBS.\n▪ TCAs\n▪ Effective in reducing abdominal pain and overall symptoms in\npatients with IBS.\n▪ SSRIs/SNRIs\n▪ Not effective in reducing abdominal pain but effective in\nimproving global IBS symptoms.\nคำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)\n• Treatment of constipation\n▪ Polyethylene glycol (PEG)\n▪ MOM, Lactulose (ED drug)\n▪ Senna, Bisacodyl (ED drug)\n▪ Evidence remains limited, Monitor for adverse effects\n▪ Soluble fiber\n▪ Effective in reducing overall symptoms in patients with IBS.\n▪ Prucalopride\n▪ Linaclotide\nคำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)\n• Treatment of diarrhea\n▪ Loperamide\n▪ Eluxadoline\n▪ ADR: sphincter of Oddi dysfunction, acute pancreatitis\n▪ Alosetron\n▪ Ramosetron\n▪ Ondansetron\n▪ Rifaximin\n▪ Cholestyramine\nคำแนะนำเกี่ยวกับโรคลำไส้แปรปรวน IBS สำหรับแพทย์ทั่วไป (แนวทำงเวชปฏิบัติ 2022)\n• CP-IBS\n▪ If fails fiber therapy as first line, use standard laxative\n(second line) for symptomatic relief\n▪ Osmotic laxative ex. Milk of Magnesia or lactulose for 4 -6\nweeks but can cause abdominal bloating and diarrhea.\n▪ Newer laxative contains propylene glycol\n▪ Avoid stimulant laxative for long -term treatment due to\nabdominal cramping and laxative dependence\n• CP-IBS\n▪ Third line: Tegaserod\n▪ Recently approve in US for women with CP- IBS\n▪ MOA: specific 5-HT4 partial agonist>> stimulate peristalic\nreflex and intestinal secretion\n▪ Dose: 6 mg BID AC for 4-6 weeks\n▪ Should be taken on an empty stomach since food decrease\nits bioavailability (by 40-65%)\n▪ ADRs: diarrhea, abdominal pain and headache\n• DP-IBS\n▪ Standard antidiarrhea\n▪ Loperamide (first line) as needed: opioid agonist >> decrease\nbowel motility\n▪ Diphenoxylate with atropine (second line): for 4-6 weeks but\n“anticholinergic adverse effect ” e.g. dry mouth, constipation,\nurinary retention\n▪ Cholestyramine (third line): 4-6 weeks, used in refractory\ncases but poorly tolerated due to palatability problems\n• DP-IBS\n▪ Alosetron\n▪ First drug approved by US FDA for specific treatment of IBS\n▪ MOA: highly potent 5-HT3 receptor antagonist >> slows\ncolonic transit time, decrease small bowel secretions\n▪ ADRs: constipation, ischemic colitis bowel perforation >>\nwithdrawal in 2000 but reintroduce with restricted conditions\n• PP-IBS\n▪ Antispasmodics\n▪ Most common prescribed are hyoscyamine and dicyclomine\n▪ Anticholinergic effect >> smooth muscle relaxant\n▪ Antidepressant\n▪ TCA for patients with severe or continuous abdominal pain\nand refractory cases\n▪ Effective at reducing both abdominal pain and diarrhea\n▪ Amitriptyline (third line): low dose 10-25 mg HS\n▪ ADRs: anticholinergic, sedative, weight gain"
            }
