              "text": "Clinical practice guideline for diagnosis and management of Parkinson's disease 2012\n• ■ Bromocriptine\n– Metabolism via CYP3A4 (dosage adjustment in\nhepatic impairment patient)\n– Drug induced pulmonary fibrosis and valvular\nheart disease (if long-term used)\n– Take with meals (decreased N/V)\n– Orthostatic hypotension\n■ Ropinirole (Metabolism via CYP3A4 and CYP1A2)\n■ Pramipexole (Dosage adjustment in renal\nimpairment patient)\n• ■ Apomorphine\n– High first pass metabolism\n– Dosage form: subcutaneous route\n– ADR: subcutaneous nodule, N/V\n• ■ Hallucination (especially in elderly or high dose)\n■ Nausea, confusion, dementia, lower-extremity\nedema, postural hypotension, sedation\n■ Serious effect include impulsive behavior\n(gambling or shopping, hypersexuality), psychosis,\nsleep attack (sudden, unexpected episode of\nsleep)\n■ Valvular heart disease and pulmonary fibrosis\n(ergot derivative is common)"
