              "pages": "หน้า 25–28",
              "text": "▪Tophus or tophi\n▪Frequent attacks (≥ 2 attacks/year)\n▪CKD stage 2 or worse\n▪Past urolithiasis\nUric acid goal\n➢ < 6 mg/dl\n➢ < 5 mg/dl for improving symptoms\nArthritis Care & Research 2012: 64(10):1431–1446.\n• ▪For patients with 1 or more subcutaneous tophi\n▪For patients with radiographic damage (any modality) attributable\nto gout\n▪For patients with frequent gout flares (≥ 2/year)\n▪For patients who have previously experienced >1 flare but have\ninfrequent flares (<2/year)\n▪For patients experiencing their first flare and CKD stage >3, SU\n>9 mg/dl\nACR GUIDELINE FOR MANAGEMENT OF GOUT 2020\nUpdate ACR 2020\n• ▪For patients experiencing their first flare\n▪For patients with asymptomatic hyperuricemia (SU >6.8 mg/dl\nwith no prior gout flares or subcutaneous tophi)\nACR GUIDELINE FOR MANAGEMENT OF GOUT 2020\nUpdate ACR 2020\nNot\nrecommended"
