              "title": "Diabetic neuropathy",
              "pages": "หน้า 22–32",
              "text": "■ Diabetic peripheral neuropathy (DPN)***\n■ Diabetic autonomic neuropathy\n■ Cardiac autonomic neuropathy\n■ Gastrointestinal neuropathies\n■ Genitourinary disturbances\nADA 2025\n• Diabetic peripheral neuropathy (DPN)***\n■ Neuropathic pain can be severe and can impact\nquality of life, limit mobility, and contribute to\ndepression and social dysfunction\nADA 2025\nGabapentinoids, serotonin norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors, tricyclic\nantidepressants, and sodium channel blockers are recommended as\ninitial pharmacologic treatments for neuropathic pain in diabetes\n• Diabetic peripheral neuropathy (DPN)***\nDiabetes Metab Res Rev 2011; 27: 629–638.\n• Clinical presentation\n■ Tingling\n■ Burning\n■ Stabbing pain\n■ Sensory loss\n■ Weakness\n■ Numbness\n■ Allodynia\n■ Hyperalgesia or hyperesthesia\n• Treatment\n■ Glycemic control\n■ Pharmacologic therapy for relives neuropathic\npain\n– Gabapentinoids, serotonin norepinephrine reuptake\ninhibitors, tricyclic antidepressants, and sodium\nchannel blockers are recommended as initial\npharmacologic treatments for neuropathic pain in\ndiabetes\nADA 2025\n• Treatment\nDiabetes Metab Res Rev 2011; 27: 629–638.\n• Treatment\nDrug class Common adverse event Major adverse event\nAnticonvulsants\n▪ Gabapentin\n▪ Pregabalin\nSomnolence, dizziness,\nataxia\nSomnolence, dizziness,\nataxia, dry mouth,\nedema, weight gain\nSJS, suicidal idea\nAngioedema, hepatotoxic,\nThrombocytopenia,\nsuicidal idea\nOpioids\n▪ Tramadol Somnolence, dizziness,\nnausea/vomiting,\nconstipation\nConfusion, seizure,\ncardiac arrhythmia\n• Treatment\nDrug class Common adverse event Major adverse event\nSNRIs\n▪ Duloxetine\n▪ Venlafaxine\nDizziness, anorexia,\nabdominal pain,\ninsomnia, loss of libido\nSomnolence, dizziness,\ndry mouth, anorexia\nHepatotoxic, GI bleeding,\nbone fracture, suicidal\nidea, delirium, cardiac\narrhythmia, myocardial\ninfraction\nTCAs\n▪ Amitriptyline\n▪ Nortriptyline\nSomnolence, headache,\ndry mouth, anorexia,\nanticholinergic side\neffect\nHepatotoxic, delirium,\nbone fracture, cardiac\narrhythmia, myocardial\ninfraction, 5-HT syndrome"
