              "text": "GLP‐1 receptor agonists\n▪ Exenatide (Byetta®, Bydureon ®)\n▪ Liraglutide (Victoza ®, Saxenda ®)\n▪ Lixisenatide (Lyxumia ®)\n▪ Albiglutide (Tanzeum ®)\n▪ Dulaglutide (Trulicity ®)\n▪ Semaglutide (Ozempic ®)\n• GLP‐1 receptor agonists\nEndocrinol Metab 2016;31:258-274\n• Nature Reviews Endocrinology volume 8, pages 728–742 (2012)\n• GLP‐1 receptor agonists\n▪ Weight loss\n▪ Rare hypoglycemia\n▪ ADR:\n▪ Nausea\n▪ Vomiting\n▪ Diarrhea\n▪ Tachycardia\n▪ Acute pancreatitis\n▪ Cholangiocarcinoma\nADA 2025.\nBlack block warning: Thyroid cell tumor\n• GLP‐1 receptor agonists\n▪ Cardiovascular benefit\n▪ Benefit on MACE\n▪ Neutral on HF\n▪ Renal benefit\n▪ Progression of CKD\nMACE, major adverse cardiovascular events\n• GLP‐1 receptor agonists\nBlack block warning: Thyroid cell tumor\n• แนวทางเวชปฏิบัติโรคเบาหวาน 2566\n• DPP‐4 inhibitors\n(Dipeptidyl peptidase IV inhibitor)\n➢ Sitagliptin (Januvia®)\n➢ Vidagliptin (Galvus®)\n➢ Saxagliptin (Onglyza®)\n➢ Linagliptin (Trajenta®)\n➢ Alogliptin (Nesina® and Vipidia®)\n• DPP‐4 inhibitors\n(Dipeptidyl peptidase IV inhibitor)\n➢ Neutral effect or decrease on weight\n➢ Rare hypoglycemia\n➢ ADR:\n▪ Angioedema/urticarial\n▪ Cholangiocarcinoma\n▪ Acute pancreatitis\n▪ Joint pain\n▪ Heart failure [Saxagliptin, Alogliptin]\nBullous Pemphigoid\n• DPP‐4 inhibitors\nดัดแปลงจาก การบริบาลทางเภสัชกรรมในผู้ป่วยเบาหวาน พ.ศ. 2558"
