              "text": "■ Allergic rhinitis involves inflammation of the\nnasal mucous membrane.\n■ This response involves the release of\ninflammatory mediators and is characterized by\nsneezing, nasal itching, and watery rhinorrhea,\noften associated with nasal congestion. Itching\nof the throat, eyes, and ears frequently\naccompanies allergic rhinitis.\nPharmacotherapy: A Pathophysiologic Approach, 10e >"
